/**
 * The site's whole icon set, as one fixed map (spec 0004, plus the four stat
 * glyphs the home page's intro band adds, the accordion's `plus` and
 * `minus` from spec 0010, and the contact cards' `headset` and `envelope`
 * from spec 0011, and the service pages' fourteen from spec 0013).
 *
 * There is no icon library. A few dozen glyphs is not enough to earn a
 * dependency, and a fixed map means `IconName` is a union over real keys: a
 * typo, or a social network nobody drew, is a type error rather than a blank
 * square at runtime. Spec 0013's glyphs are copied into the map from open
 * licence sets instead of drawn here, each with a comment naming its set,
 * source glyph, and licence; `src/assets/images/CREDITS.md` lists them too.
 *
 * Every glyph is drawn on the same 24 unit grid and inherits `currentColor`,
 * so an icon is coloured by the text around it and never names a colour of its
 * own. That is also why `--color-yellow` stays unused by this feature.
 *
 * Icons are decorative by default and hidden from assistive tech. Pass `title`
 * only when the icon is the whole accessible name of a control, as the footer's
 * social links do.
 */

/**
 * Interface glyphs are drawn as strokes so they stay optically even at any
 * size; the social marks are solid brand shapes and have to be filled.
 *
 * `evenodd` is for a filled glyph whose details are holes punched through it
 * (a clock's hands, a building's windows): under the even odd rule a shape
 * drawn inside another cuts it out, whichever direction it was drawn in.
 */
type IconDef = Readonly<{
  d: string;
  mode: 'stroke' | 'fill';
  evenodd?: true;
}>;

